From 400f2c4fe9c1589c86f93899aeb6469ca55c8581 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: exploitizm <351399878+exploitizm@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 15:13:06 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 12/14] radv/ps5: mesh shaders without a task shader run as
 compute too

Run 15:07 on the Lichii 09b78bd2df core: the GPU stopped 101 s in at a mesh
draw without a task shader (DRAW_INDEX_AUTO of 78, a vertex a mesh
workgroup), which never reached its end-of-pipe event: the NGG mesh launch
hang mesh compute avoids, on the path it did not take.

Such a pipeline runs its mesh shader as compute now as well: the records
pass reads the draws' own commands (the direct draw's grid, uploaded as
one) and gives each record its draw's ID (draw_id_step), the task
emulation's records hold them, and the passes are the same. Mesh pipelines
the path does not take are logged with the reason, for the first 16. The
cache's UUID takes the path's version, so pipelines cached on the hardware
path are not taken.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
